# Hashed 2026-10-28 (UTC) on AWS (c8g.2xlarge, us-west-2), streaming each object where it lives (aws s3 cp <obj> - | sha256sum, CRT client); bytes read == the object's ContentLength for every row. This was AFTER the consuming measurement's runs: it proves today's bytes, not necessarily the bytes the run read.
# terra reference CSVs, one pair per chip prefix; read by geo-ml-real (each chip its own). Every hash equals the one geo-ml-real's run recorded as it read the file (results/<chip>/results.json: terra_tract_areas_sha256, terra_zonal_sha256), so these are the run's bytes.
